    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d882">

                <pb facs="0818" n="718" xml:id="pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">661.1115/101: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Denmark</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extracts]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-07-12T16:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 12, 1920—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:26 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>15. Referring to the Department’s telegram of 7th<anchor n="8" xml:id="d882-f1"/>
                    regarding removal of trade restrictions with Soviet Russia. Is railway equipment
                    regarded as war material?</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Would be glad to have such information as Department can give me regarding its
                    attitude toward the eventual use of that Copenhagen clearing house by American
                    concerns. See my 6, May [<hi rendition="#italic">June?</hi>] 19, 2 p.m.<anchor
                        n="9" xml:id="d882-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d882-f1" n="8" xml:id="d882-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram no. 1215, July 7, to the Ambassador in France, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra</hi>, was repeated to the Minister in Denmark.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d882-f2" n="9" xml:id="d882-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
